	(text_box "CONTROLLED IMPEDANCE TRACE WIDTHS\n(Simulations done using ADS Controlled Impedance Line Designer)\n- Simulated is JLCPCB: JLC04161H-3313(Finished thickness1.56mm±10%)\n\n1. Microstrip Edge Coupled, 100 Ohm Differential Impedance, 0.35mm (center to center), 50mmm Length, f=1Ghz, Width = 0.1225 mm\n2. Coplanar Edge Coupled, 100 Ohm Differential Impedance, 0.35mm (center to center), 0.25mm Clearance, 50mmm Length, f=1Ghz, Width = 0.1354 mm, 0.35 - 0.1354 = 0.2146 mm (edge to edge spacing)\n3. USB Coplanar Edge Coupled, 90 Ohm Differential Impedance, 0.5mm (center to center), 0.25mm Clearance, 50mmm Length, f=240Mhz, Width = 0.1704 mm, 0.5 - 0.1704 = 0.3296 mm\n4. USB Microstrip Edge Coupled, 90 Ohm Differential Impedance, 0.5mm (center to center), 50mmm Length, f=240Mhz, Width = 0.1722 mm\n\nRF TRACE 50 Ohm\n- Coplanar single-ended , f is 2.5 GHz, L 20mm, Clearance 0.25mm, Width = 0.1472 mm\n- Coplanar single-ended , f is 5 GHz, L 20mm, Clearance 0.25mm, Width = 0.1475 mm\n\n\nSMA CONNECTOR SIGNAL PIN (MIDDLE) FOOTPRINT\n- With normal 0.35 mm clearance resulted in a veryy significant signal degradation\n- I recalculated the clearance for the middle pin using ADS:\n  - Coplanar Single-Ended, Length: 5mm, Width: 1.37 mmm (width of the pin), f: 5GHz, Clearance = 0.4046 mm\n\nESP32C5 DESIGN CONSIDERATIONS:\n- Flash memory traces NOT length matched. (at 80 MHz not needed)\n- Isolate the CLK trace on the ext flash memory bus\n\nCAN-FD INTERFACE:\n- Two parallel CAN-FD interfaces in the single connector (each row)\n- 120 Ohm shunted across CANH and CANL (to be done on the receiver and sender) \n- A 10u capacitor has been added on the shield pins.\n  - Both shield pins connected\n  - Capacitor is to be replaced by GND jumper at primary node \n\nSERIES TERMINATION\n- CSI, DSI, SDIO (near P4), UART0, UART1, NOT I2C\nSDIO\n- Array Series termination on SDIO DATA 0-3\n- Individual series termination on CLK, CMD\n- PU on the SDIO INT (Interrupt) pin (Open Drain)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
