	(text_box "POWER MANAGEMENT NOTES:\n- The input power goes through three stages \n  1. a) External Power: LM73100RPWR, 2.7 - 23 V, 5.5 A Integrated Ideal Diode with Input Reverse Polarity and Overvoltage Protection\n     b) USB POWER: SS34-E3/57T Diode\n  2. TPS259531DSGR 2.7V to 18V, 4-A, 34-mΩ eFuse With Fast Overvoltage Protection\n  3. TPS62442RQRR, 2.75-V to 6-V, Dual-Channel Step-Down Converter with Adjustable Frequency\n\n- Stage Description:\n  1. The power is sourced from the imediatelly connected power source without relying on jumpers to manual selection. The diodes prevent current from flowing back to a source in case of multiple ppower sources being conected.\n     The ideal diode was used for thhe external power source to limit power loss inherent in a regular diode as the eternal power source will at times be a battery.   \n     The ideal diode includes ppolarity protection (not required on the USB sources)\n  2. The eFuse provides overvoltage protection, undervoltage lockout, Short Circuit Protection, and limits inrussh current.\n  3. SMPS that outputs two power rails. The first is dedicated and controlled by the ESP32P4 core. The second is general 3.3V power rail used by all other components.\n\nESP32P4 Power Domains\n- THE VDD_HP pins: 600mA to 1A Current, Required Width: 0.3 mm (1A)\n\nIdeal Diode LM73100RPWR Parameter Notes:\n- Maximum System Peak Current (IOUT): 2.5 A (to cleanly capture joint ESP32 radio bursts, camera operations, and converter losses).\n- I IMON is not used (connected to GND), no monitoring pins available on the MCU\n- Calculate the Value for RIMON = VADC_MAX/IIMON = 3.3 V/452.5 μA ≈ 7.29 kΩ IMON\n​\nEFUSE TPS259531DSGR Notes:\n- Short circuit protection/current limiter\n- Max current: R ILM = 387 Ohms (500 Ohm) at 4.17 A\n- Over Voltage Clamp (OVC) set at 5.7V (for TPS25953x)\n\nSMPS TPS62442RQRR Notes:\n- The PG1 and PG2 left floatng as they are not used. The MCU PU pins are handled through a parallel C. \n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
