	(text_box "ESP32P4 HARDWARE CONSIDERATIONS:\n- DEBUG\n  - The P4 has both USB ports exposed and the UART0 as a last resort debug.\n  - Main flash/debug is to be done through the USB/JTAG port\n  - The MCU JTAG pins are exposed on a header but do not include the PU and PD resistors.\n- BOOT CONFIGURATION\n  - \n\n- CSI_LDO-CE Pin on the CAMERA turns the internal camera LDO ON or OFF thereby alowing the chip to turn it off when not needed (in sleep mode)\n- CSI_FLASH-LED pin is a CAMERA output pinn that is designed to send ouput signal to a flash to iluminate the surounding at the exact time of image capture\n  (Will not be used NC)\n\n- RESET CIRCUT\n  - The goal is for the ESP32P4 to reset from global reset pin, but also to reset after a firmware update without causing global reset of other devices.\n  - Implementation: GLOBAL RESET is connected through a buffer to the MCU that only pulls reset LOW and is HIGH-Z otherwise. The MCU RST (PU) pin is exposed with the JTAG pins on a headder to allow RST after upload.\n  - PU (RST) Timing Considerations: The PU has to stay low for tSTBL = 50uS after VIN stable at 3.3V\n    - Place a 100nF capacitor at PU."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
