	(text_box "ESP32P4 SETUP NOTES:\n1. The PARLIO (Parallel interface) pins are set as general PARLIO IO to be set up with specific pin functtiin throuugh the GPIO Matrix. The function of each PARLIO pin can be determined based on the target device.\n2. GPIO45 is to be set up as CINT (SDIO Interrupt) for the ESP32C5 to let the P4 know of available information on the SDIO bus.\n3. The W25Q256JWPIQ flash memory is a 1.8V device and is powered as well as logic I/O from VDDO_FLASH (PIN71). Set up logic 1.8V output before connecting. Set the EFUSE_0PXA_TIEH_SEL_0 register.\n   (DO NOT solder on the flash until the flash votage is set to 1.8V)\n4. VDD_HP_n is CORE power with 1.3V MAX. Set to 1.2V (as per reference)\n5. BOOT CONFIGURATION\n   - The ESP32P4 can be programmed using USB-Serial-JTAG Download\n     (The USB Serial/JTAG Controller is able to put the ESP32-P4 into download mode automatically - NO NEED TO PULL GPIO35 LOW MANUALLY)\n   - GPIO35 HIGH: SPI Boot mode (default), PU is permanently on GPIO35\n   - GPIO35 LOW: Joint Download Boot mode (USB-Serial-JTAG Download Boot, UART Download Boot, SPI Slave Download Boot, USB 2.0 OTG Download)\n   - JTAG Signal Source Control\n     - eFuse 3: EFUSE_JTAG_SEL_ENABLE to 1\n     - GPIO34 can be used for JTAG signal source\n       - 1: JTAG signals come from USB Serial/JTAG Controller\n       - 0: JTAG signals come from corresponding pins MTDI, MTCK, MTMS, and MTDO\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
